### Research trail (why this is excluded)

1. Four web searches on 2026-10-27 (exact-phrase `qwen3.5-flash-lite` model studio pricing; `"Qwen3.5-Flash-Lite" OR "Qwen3.5 Flash Lite" benchmark OpenRouter`; Qwen 3.5 series lineup; Qwen flash-lite across 3.5/3.6/3.7 generations) surfaced **zero** occurrences of the exact model in: Alibaba Cloud Model Studio pricing and supported-models pages (updated 2026-10-11), the official @Alibaba_Qwen series announcement, BenchLM's Alibaba release timeline (36 confirmed releases — Plus and Flash exist, no Lite), OpenRouter, llm-stats, DFO, pricepertoken, aimlapi, orq.ai, Requesty, and eesel.
2. **Likely slug-contamination source:** the "-Flash-Lite" naming in this era belongs to Google (`gemini-3.5-flash-lite`, released 2026-07-21, and `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`) — both separately tracked in this repo. Combined with the real `qwen3.5-flash` tier, the compound "Qwen3.5-Flash-Lite" appears to be a roster conflation, not a vendor product.
3. The real Qwen budget tiers below Qwen3.5-Flash are its **open-weight siblings** (Qwen3.5-35B-A3B / 27B / 122B-A10B / 397B-A17B and the small dense 12B/4B/2B/0.8B line), not a hosted "Lite" API.
4. Per contract: zero verified public benchmark numbers → `.md.excluded`, never invented numbers. The pre-existing `average.md` in this folder (score 75.6) could not have come from a real `qwen3.5-flash-lite` evaluation and should be reviewed by the project owner.

